  ==========================================================================

  *** Installation ***

  After installing the files, the following steps should be taken:

   1. This is a NO MSG module.  All changes can be made online!
   2. Add "HotKeys" to your menu tree.
      Add this where normal users can get to it as well, so they can
      modify their Personal HotKeys.
   3. All done! BBS GO!

  ==========================================================================

  *** What are HotKeys? ***

      HotKeys make your bbs easier to navigate.  Long command lines, can
    be compacted down and mapped to one control-key sequence!  These
    commands will make it easier and faster to move around your system
    as well as handle any other tasks you wish them to handle.

      HotKeys also is an invaluable command line tool.  HotKeys allow you
    to abort what you are currently typing by hitting the <ESC> key.  You
    can redraw your current line of input using the CTRL-R sequence.  You
    can even change the foreground & background color of what you are
    typing!

  ==========================================================================

  *** Some Miscellaneous Notes ***

   . HotKey CTRL-J is system reserved.  On our system we have found
     that some users' terminals send CTRL-J's while they are telnetting in.
     In most cases, it works fine for all users, except for users who are
     telnetting in (CTRL-J is the only one we have found which does not work
     in all cases).  This sequence is now mapped to disable HotKeys.

   . HotKeys works by changing the users character interceptor.  If a module
     you use changes a users character interceptor, they will NOT have access
     to HotKeys until they exit that module back to a point where HotKeys
     can safely re-enable itself on the users line.

