  Version 1.0b - May 11, 1996:
   . First beta release.

  Version 1.1b - June 1, 1996:
   . Fixed it so CURSOR movements do not spit out "garbage" when pressed.
   . Added a HOTKEY to turn off hotkeys.  I used CTRL-J because this
     has caused problems with certain terminal programs.

  Version 1.2 - July 10, 1996:
   . Demos expire in 2 weeks.

  Version 2.0 - November 12, 1996
   . HotKeys is now NO MSG compliant!
   . Moved HotKeys configuration to a Btrieve database instead of
     the DIALHOT.CFG text file.

  Version 2.1 - May 18, 1997
   . Added option to turn off logon advertisement.

  Version 2.5 - June 14, 1997
   . Added ability for users to create personal HotKeys.  Each user
     can now redefine keys !,@,#,$,%,^,&,*,(,) for personal HotKeys.

   . Added global commands:
      /HOTKEYS  ...  Shows System Defined HotKeys
      /HOTON    ...  Enable HotKeys
      /HOTOFF   ...  Disable HotKeys
      /HOTLIST  ...  List your Personal HotKeys
    All of these commands can be modified in CONFIG.

  Version 2.6 - July 10, 1997
   . WorldGroup 3.0 DOS Port.

  Version 2.7
   . Migrated build system to Microsoft Visual Studio 2022.
   . Ported to The Major BBS v10.
   . Released as open-source under the MIT License.
   . Removed commercial licensing system.

